<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">Interest Coverage Ratio  nQuarter end Sept 30 2019 is 58.3  nYTD is 59.69  nNotes  nThe unaudited consolidated financial results-UCFR include financial results of AETL - Holding Co &amp; financial results of subsidiary companies, ABAT, AESL, JC Biotech, Advanced EnzymesUSA Inc, Cal India Foods International USA Advanced Supplementary Technologies Corporation USA, Enzyme Innovation Inc USA, Dynamic Enzymes, Inc USA, Advanced Enzymes Malaysia-AEM, Advanced Enzymes Europe &amp; evoxx Technologies GmbH Germany. Holding Company &amp; its subsidiary cos constitute the Group  nThe above UCFR were reviewed by Audit Comm &amp; approved by Board on 2 Nov 19.Above results have been subjected to limited review(LR) by statutory auditors &amp; they have expressed an unmodified opinion.LR report will be filed with stock exchanges &amp; will be available on the Company website.Results prepared in accordance with IND AS prescribed under Section 133 of the Companies Act, 2013 &amp; other recognised accounting practices &amp; policies to the extent applicable  nGroup operates only in 1 primary business segment viz manufacturing &amp; sales of enzymes  nDuring quarter ended 30 Sept 19 Company has allotted 8,400 equity shares (ES) to employees under AETL Employee Stock Option Scheme 2015-AETL ESOS 2015 &amp; during 6 months then ended Company has allotted 27500 ES to employees under AETL ESOS 2015  nGroup has adopted IndAS 116 Leases effective annual reporting period beginning 1 Apr 19 &amp; applied the standard to its leases using modified retrospective approach.Accordingly the Group is not required to restate comparative information for previous Year/Period. There is no impact of adoption of Ind AS 116 to retained earnings as at 1 Apr 19  nGroup has recognised a lease liability of Rs.150.69 million (mn) &amp; corresponding RightOfUse–ROU-asset on  date of transition ie. 1 Apr 19  nMajor impact of adopting Ind AS 116 on Group UCFR for quarter &amp; 6 months ended 30 Sept 19 is as follows  nDepreciation &amp; amortisation expenses has increased by Rs. 13.29 &amp; Rs. 24.91mn for quarter &amp; six months ended 30 Sept 19 respectively, due to amortisation of ROU asset  nFinance cost has increased by Rs. 2.50 &amp; Rs. 4.60mn for quarter &amp; six months ended 30 Sept 19 respectively, due to interest accrued on o/s lease liability  nRent expense has decreased by Rs11.23 &amp; Rs23.15 mn for quarter &amp; 6 months ended 30 Sept 19 respt due to recognition of operating lease as ROU asset &amp; a corresponding lease liability  nCompany &amp; 1 of its subsidiary viz. JCB has decided to exercise option u/s 115BAA of Income Tax Act 1961 as introduced by taxation Laws Amendment Ordinance, 2019 from subsequent FY. Accordingly there is no impact on provision for income tax for quarter &amp; 6 months ended 30 Sept 19. These 2 cos expect to reverse deferred tax liabilities partly in current FY &amp; partly in subsequent years. Accordingly, deferred tax balances have been re-measured using tax rate expected to be prevalent in the period in which deferred tax balances are expected to reverse, &amp;  resultant impact shall be recognised in statement of profit &amp; loss over 3 quarters including current quarter of FY20  nABAT &amp; AESL subsidiaries of Company has decided to exercise option permitted under Sec 115BAA of Income Tax Act 1961 as introduced by taxation Laws Amendment Ordinance, 2019 from current FY.Accordingly the provision for income tax &amp; deferred tax balances have been RecordedRemeasured using new tax rate &amp; resultant impact has been recognised in current period Statement of Profit &amp; Loss  nThe Group has discontinued operations of 1 of its subsidiary AEM &amp; goodwill on acquisition of AEM amounting to Rs. 0.93 mn has been written off. Company will initiate procedure for winding up of AEM  nShareholders in its meeting of 8 Aug 19 approved final dividend for FY19 of Rs 0.60 per ES &amp; same was paid on 13 Aug 19</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
